## 2. Map Editor

### 2.1 Purpose

The Map Editor is used to create and modify:

- Maps
- Rooms
- Room connections
- Room types and colors
- Room contents (items, merchants)

It is the primary tool for building the physical world layout.

### 2.2 Editable Properties

**Room metadata**

- `room.name`
- `room.description`
- `room.x`, `room.y` (coordinates on the map grid)
- `room.map_id`
- `room.room_type`  
  - `normal`, `merchant`, `bank`, `warehouse`, `factory`, etc.
- `room.factory_tier` (for factory rooms)
- `room_type_colors` mapping (visual cues in UI)

**Map-level properties**

- `map.name`
- `map.description`
- `map.width`
- `map.height`

**Connections**

- `connected_map_id`
- `connected_room_x`
- `connected_room_y`
- `connection_direction` (N, S, E, W, NE, NW, SE, SW, U, D)

**Room content**

- Room items (add/remove/clear)
- Merchant inventory in that room

### 2.3 Database Tables

- `rooms` — Room metadata and types
- `maps` — Map definitions and dimensions
- `room_type_colors` — Visual color mapping for room types
- `room_items` — Items placed in rooms
- `merchant_items` — Merchant inventory configuration

