## 5. Item Editor

### 5.1 Purpose

The Item Editor is used to define and maintain:

- Base item definitions
- Rune properties
- Deed properties (warehouse deed, etc.)
- Merchant inventory assignments

It is the foundation for all item-based systems (inventory, factory, warehouse, merchants).

### 5.2 Editable Properties

**Base properties**

- `name`
- `description`
- `item_type` (`ingredient`, `rune`, `deed`, etc.)
- `active`
- `poofable` (whether it can be removed/cleaned up)
- `encumbrance`

**Deed properties** (for `item_type = 'deed'`)

- `deed_warehouse_location_key`
- `deed_base_max_item_types`
- `deed_max_total_items`
- `deed_automation_enabled`

**Rune properties** (for `item_type = 'rune'`)

- `rune_color`
- `rune_type` (e.g., `PRODUCTION`, `SPEED`, `EFFICIENCY`)

**Merchant configuration**

- Assign/remove items to merchants in specific rooms
- Configure merchant inventory entries

### 5.3 Database Tables

- `items` — Core item definitions
- `merchant_items` — Merchant inventory (managed via Item/Map tools)

