## 7. Ticket Editor

### 7.1 Purpose

The Ticket Editor is your in-game two-way communication and work-tracking tool between:

- You / other god-mode players
- Cursor / AI
- The codebase roadmap

It’s how you log bugs, ideas, and feature requests from inside the game.

> **Access:**  
> The Ticket Editor is accessed via the `Z` key in the command line, *not* via the God Widget, but still requires `flag_god_mode = 1`.

### 7.2 Editable Properties

- `title`
- `description`
- `reproSteps`
- `status` (`open`, `backlog`, `in_progress`, `resolved`)
- `priority` (`1 = low`, `2 = medium`, `3 = high`, `4 = critical`)
- `ticket_type` (`debug`, `manual`, `user`)
- `estimated_effort` (`quick`, `medium`, `complex`)
- `tags` (array)
- `environment` (JSON)
- `logs` (JSON)
- `resolution_notes`
- `player_id` / `player_name` (who created or owns it)

### 7.3 Database Tables

- `debug_todos` — Tickets/todos stored as structured records

